Z||000000||Wade87GT||05-20-2001||07:52 PM||||Hey all, I need some ideas please. When I'm going through a right hand curve, above 20 mph, I hear a droning sound coming from the right rear. I jacked up the car and checked everything. No free play when I shake the wheels or unusual sounds when I rotate them. The cv joints seem OK too. I have 156,000 miles on my 5-speed GT and I should probably replace the cv joint/axel assembly and the rear bearings. Are all rebuilt assemblys the same, quality wise?<P>Wade||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||05-21-2001||01:15 AM||||Could be a wheel bearing. If it is noisey on one turn and quiet on  the opposite turn, that's a indication of a bad wheel bearing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||05-21-2001||05:52 PM||||Here's an irrelevant point. A droning sound on a car with an automatic could be the TCC lockup. Find out by unplugging it.<P>Just thought someone reading this thread might benefit.||||reg||1
